  "releaseNotes": "Unit properties that refuse no value are marked required\nPreserve instrument steps and quoted liquidity in market emulation\nMarket emulator: a subscriber to the order log gets its rows\nUnwind the blocking waits left by the async rework and fix what it uncovered\nMark the blocking wrappers obsolete\nAdd walk-forward optimization, a market profile, three statistics and candle spread options\nMove instrument lookups and persistence to async\nReport the emulated account to the connector, floating profit included\nEmulation: stop the clock check refusing requests, and the book improving on a resting order\nEmulation: take an order that is stamped behind the feed\nHand a finished bar over when it closes, not when it opened\nReplay a closed day at that day, not at the run's first moment\nFix matching engine and emulation lifecycles",
